@meta
id: 01-08
title: Ctrl-C and Escape are not twins
chapter: 01
type: lesson
skills: esc, mode-awareness, cmdline, insert-i
par: 14
minutes: 4
vscode: Ctrl-C copies — here it does nothing of the kind
open: config.ts

@brief
`Esc` is a long way from the home row, and sooner or later somebody tells
you that `Ctrl-C` does the same job. Nearly. It leaves insert mode, it
cancels a half-typed command line, and it interrupts a command that is
taking too long.

What it skips is the tidying up vim does on the way out of insert mode:
abbreviations do not expand, and anything configured to run when insert
mode ends does not run. In a plain vim you will not notice. In a vim with
a plugin or two, you will, and it will look like the plugin is broken.

The timeout in config.ts is ten times too small. It should be `300`.
Make the change, and this once leave insert mode with `Ctrl-C` instead of
`Esc` so you have felt the difference.

@keys
| `Ctrl-C` | leave insert mode, skipping the usual exit work |
| `Ctrl-C` | on the command line, cancel it |
| `Esc` | leave insert mode properly |

@hints
`$` lands on the last character of the line, which is the comma. You want
to type to the left of it.
--
`i` inserts before the character the cursor is on. One character is all
you are adding.
--
`jj` to the timeout line, `$`, `i`, the new digit, then `Ctrl-C`, then
save and quit.

@solution
    j j $ i 0 <Ctrl-C> :wq<Enter>

Use `Esc`. That is the honest recommendation. `Ctrl-C` is the right key in
exactly one common situation — a command that has run away from you, a
search over a huge file or a mistaken `:g`, where it is the interrupt and
`Esc` is not.

The wider point is that vim gives you more than one way out of a mode and
they differ in the details. `Esc`, `Ctrl-C` and `Ctrl-[` all get you to
normal mode; `Ctrl-[` is `Esc` exactly, the same byte on the wire, which
is why some people use it and never reach for the far corner of the
keyboard.

@start config.ts
export const config = {
  port: 4000,
  timeout: 30,
};

@expected config.ts
export const config = {
  port: 4000,
  timeout: 300,
};
